DevOps – Jenkins

Jenkins Webhooks — a powerful way to trigger builds automatically whenever code is pushed to a repository like GitHub or GitLab.

🔹 Instead of manually starting builds, webhooks make Jenkins event-driven.
🔹 This reduces delays and ensures code changes are tested instantly.
🔹 Common use: GitHub → Jenkins Pipeline → Automated Build & Test → Deployment.

Key takeaway: Webhooks turn Jenkins into a real-time CI/CD automation engine.
